{:edb/db-before-t 2373 :edb/db-after-t 2374 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535686 50 #inst "2026-10-09T05:11:22.288Z" 13194139535686 true] [17592186133704 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361127 13194139535686 true] [17592186133705 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361134 13194139535686 true] [17592186133705 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361148 13194139535686 true] [17592186133760 1020 #edb/ref 17592186361141 13194139535686 true] [17592186134208 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535686 true] [17592186134208 1100 "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\n- $U={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $V={[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $W={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186134208 1100 "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\n1. $U = {\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$\n2. $V = {\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}$\n3. $W = {\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}}$" 13194139535686 false] [17592186134208 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$\n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}}$, respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+0=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=1+0=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0+1=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0+0=0\\ne 1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=0-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}=-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\ne 0 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ only\"." 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361128 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1089 "q-140483" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1100 "Which of the following sets are orthonormal?\n\n- $U={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $V={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}$\n- $W={[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1113 #uuid "0319c98a-c0c2-5975-94ee-3cc2f04ae409" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361127 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of the given sets as \n${{u}_{1},{u}_{2}},$ \n${{v}_{1},{v}_{2}},$ and \n${{w}_{1},{w}_{2}},$ respectively. \n\nThe sets $U,V,$ and $W$ are orthonormal if the following conditions on each set hold:\n\n- ${u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1}=1 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${v}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1}=1 \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\n- ${w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2}=0\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{1}=1 \\\\ {w}_{2}\\cdot {w}_{2}=1.\\end{aligned}$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- For the set $U,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{1}\\cdot {u}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot {u}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the set $U$ is orthonormal.\n\n- For the set $V,$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}}+0-\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt{5}}=0 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{1}\\cdot {v}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{4}{9}+\\frac{4}{9}=1 & ✓ \\\\ {v}_{2}\\cdot {v}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=\\frac{4}{5}+\\frac{1}{5}=1 & ✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $V$ is an orthonormal set.\n\n- For the set $W,$ notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{w}_{1}\\cdot {w}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]=-\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}=-1 & \\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $W$ is not an orthonormal set.\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"$U$ and $V$ only\"." 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361129 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361130 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361131 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361132 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361133 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1041 "selection" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361130 13194139535686 true] [17592186361128 1110 #uuid "d56fdc5b-d55c-57d2-839e-771468d8c222" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361129 1034 "$V$ only" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361129 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535686 true] [17592186361129 1111 #uuid "1453f428-400b-57b9-bbde-d5ddfe9fe6ae" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361130 1034 "$U$ and $V$ only" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361130 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535686 true] [17592186361130 1111 #uuid "0716477b-2ed8-5de6-a2c4-84a50075a95d" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361131 1034 "$U,V,$ and $W$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361131 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535686 true] [17592186361131 1111 #uuid "fba8d1a5-8d3f-5f75-8b1e-2d3f8da3c4f0" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361132 1034 "$W$ and $V$ only" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361132 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535686 true] [17592186361132 1111 #uuid "89e86bd4-9a4e-579b-b0f9-287c18de3a09" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361133 1034 "$W$ only" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361133 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535686 true] [17592186361133 1111 #uuid "279a7498-363f-57e2-bdf6-4eda864661b9" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361135 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1089 "q-40399" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1100 "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}?$\n\n$$\nU={[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]}\n$$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1113 #uuid "cde9f38e-3e07-575b-bde6-6b039505af2a" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361134 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$, we need to find a third vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-6{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -6 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-\\frac{1}{6}){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}6 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -\\frac{37}{6} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns ($1$st and $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we get ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{37}{6}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{1}+{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{6}{x}_{3} \\\\ -\\frac{37}{6}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{3}=6$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -37 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{3}$ is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -37 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{1}{37}.$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361136 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361137 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361138 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361139 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361140 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1041 "selection" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361136 13194139535686 true] [17592186361135 1110 #uuid "de65cdc7-8225-560a-a563-ab6a5e15520d" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361136 1034 "\\frac{1}{37}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361136 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361136 1111 #uuid "537b751d-bb9a-5ed5-80fe-9e1268333e8c" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361137 1034 "-\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361137 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361137 1111 #uuid "a5f652c9-c4c1-5808-84e0-03c42ba2b747" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361138 1034 "\\frac{1}{35}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361138 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361138 1111 #uuid "cd398ffa-d85f-5780-9412-658d76d758fd" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361139 1034 "\\frac{1}{6}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361139 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361139 1111 #uuid "20a1e346-29ed-5d6d-9017-db8fb6ed5635" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361140 1034 "\\frac{35}{6}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361140 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361140 1111 #uuid "aae5bbf6-54e8-5104-9a03-3afd948fdbcf" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361142 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1089 "q-81115" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1100 "Consider the **orthonormal** set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an **orthonormal** basis of ${R}^{2}.$ What is the value of $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|?$\n\n$$\nU={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}\n$$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1113 #uuid "6f777aef-9696-5253-bf86-55547e1a8ff5" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361141 1145 "Let's denote the vector of $U$ as ${u}_{1}.$ To extend the given set to an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$, we need to find a second vector $x$ such that $‖x‖=1,$ and\n\n$$\n{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0\\,⟹\\,\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{1}+\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}{x}_{2}=0.\n$$\n\nFrom the above equation, we get ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2}.$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2}{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{2}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{2}=-2,$ we obtain the vector \n$x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nNow, we need to normalize $x.$ Notice that $‖x‖=\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=\\sqrt{5}.$ So, we normalize $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x}{‖x‖}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthonormal basis of ${R}^{2}$ is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $|{x}_{1}|+|{x}_{2}|=|\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}|+|-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}|=\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}.$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361143 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361144 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361145 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361146 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361147 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1041 "selection" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361144 13194139535686 true] [17592186361142 1110 #uuid "a9a71385-2384-59de-96e3-8a6eafbfc9c8" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361143 1034 "\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361143 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361143 1111 #uuid "e55437d6-3124-585b-a796-a4ea12e9d684" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361144 1034 "\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361144 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361144 1111 #uuid "69099f33-4226-567e-af28-7b269c2a62e9" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361145 1034 "\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361145 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361145 1111 #uuid "2a2e19fa-0b16-5249-835f-d9f0187478c6" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361146 1034 "3\\sqrt{5}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361146 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361146 1111 #uuid "42837190-3851-55da-a933-6bf00f7cc545" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361147 1034 "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361147 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361147 1111 #uuid "ca3a544f-0cda-5730-a7d6-1fc083df5f8a" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1017 #edb/ref 17592186361149 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1089 "q-83749" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1100 "Consider the orthogonal set $U$ below. By adding a new vector $x=[{x}_{1},\\,{x}_{2},\\,{x}_{3},\\,{x}_{4}]^{T},$ extend the set so that it forms an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}.$ What is the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}?$\n\n$$\nU={[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}\n$$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1113 #uuid "1d20e935-b799-5f33-a56d-d5db4d639df5" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361148 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $U$ as ${u}_{1},\\,{u}_{2},\\,{u}_{3}.$ To extend the given set to an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$, we need to find a fourth vector $x$ such that\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{u}_{1}\\cdot x=0 \\\\ {u}_{2}\\cdot x=0 \\\\ {u}_{3}\\cdot x=0\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}+2{x}_{4}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}+3{x}_{4}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the augmented matrix $M$ of the system above and reduce it to its row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 4 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are three pivot columns ($1$st, $2$nd and $3$rd). Thus, ${x}_{4}$ is a free variable. From the third and first equation, we get ${x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4}$ and ${x}_{1}={x}_{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4}$, respectively. Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2}-4(-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4})+2{x}_{4}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=-\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{5}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}{x}_{4} \\\\ {x}_{4}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{4}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting ${x}_{4}=3$, we obtain the vector \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, an orthogonal basis of ${R}^{4}$ is\n\n$$\n{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}.\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\,\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{4}}=\\frac{-1}{3}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361150 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361151 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361152 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361153 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1000 #edb/ref 17592186361154 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1041 "selection" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1104 #edb/ref 17592186361151 13194139535686 true] [17592186361149 1110 #uuid "4b8cd294-0c07-5f86-b5cb-8ac1dc4ecc68" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361150 1034 "-\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361150 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361150 1111 #uuid "0ef89e50-69b3-58c5-af25-976018ae32a0" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361151 1034 "-\\frac{1}{3}" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361151 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361151 1111 #uuid "e318ab04-fda8-508c-97eb-cfb5c0fc9c01" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361152 1034 "1" 13194139535686 true] [17592186361152 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535686 true] [17592186361152 1111 #uuid "e19eeb7c-9357-5435-98b5-16005352361f" 131